# Aider Studio (auto-added)
REPO_MAP.md
.aider/
/.tick
# NOTE: `/phases` used to be listed here. It is now governed by the block further down
# ("Internal PDDA/agent phase mechanics"). Re-adding it here would silently kill that block's
# negations, because git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded.

# Public-release sanitization scanner output (utils/sanitize-scan.sh)
.sanitize-findings.tsv
.sanitize-tmp/

# --- Public-release sanitization: quarantined paths (branch public/release-candidate-01) ---
# These were tracked and have been untracked + moved to temp/moved-private-files/.
# Ignored here so they cannot silently drift back into the index on a later commit.
# See temp/moved-private-files/SANITIZATION-PLAN.md and moved-files.md.

# Raw AI reviewer transcripts — internal harness output, high leak surface (decision E8)
#
# NARROWED 2026-08-07 (operator decision, knowingly reversing part of E8): marathon-drive commits a
# per-phase transcript here and HALTs the phase if it cannot. Only that file is tracked; every other
# relay-system artifact stays ignored, so E8 still holds for ad-hoc /relay threads and preflight.
# The published surface is builder/reviewer turn output on a PUBLIC repo — that is the accepted cost
# of running marathons here. If that stops being acceptable, restore the bare `relay-system/` line
# and run marathons somewhere the harness can track its own output.
relay-system/*
!relay-system/*/
relay-system/*/*
!relay-system/*/marathon-*.md

# RAG index: a searchable embedding of the ENTIRE codebase + docs. Regenerable build
# artifact, and it re-leaks anything scrubbed elsewhere. Must never be committed.
data/rag/*.sqlite
data/rag/*.sqlite-journal
data/rag/*.db

# Real production reminder dumps and counters (workspace data, client names, people)
temp/*_reminders.json
temp/*_reminder_counter.json
*_reminders.production.json

# Internal PDDA/agent phase mechanics — dropped from the public repo (Q2b, agy concurred).
#
# NARROWED 2026-08-07 (operator decision, knowingly reversing part of Q2b): marathon-drive hard-
# requires `git add` of BOTH files below — RELAY.md is the relay audit trail and ESCALATION.md is
# written on the halt path — and it HALTs the phase if either cannot be committed. The live harness
# behaves identically, so `xyz-sync --update` does not avoid this.
#
# Track ONLY those two files; all other phase artifacts stay ignored. Note the `phases/*` form: git
# cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, so a bare `phases/` would make every
# negation below a dead letter — and there is a second `/phases` entry up in the Aider block that
# must stay removed for the same reason.
phases/*
!phases/*/
phases/*/*
!phases/*/RELAY.md
!phases/*/ESCALATION.md
xyz-tick/

# Internal-only docs dropped from the public repo (front-door audit, 2026-07-26)
4X4.md
AGENTS-PROPOSED.md
AI-TRIAGE.md
ASKCODE_INTEGRATION_COPY.md
DASHBOARD.md
PIPELINE.md
SKILL-DEBUG.md
docs/SLEUTH-PRODUCT-ONBOARDING-GUIDE.md
docs/session-summary-*.md
docs/incident-report-*.md

# Internal deploy/ops CI — never ships publicly. Self-hosted runners on a public repo are
# an RCE vector (fork PRs execute on your runner), and these leak deploy topology + secret names.
.github/workflows/cicd.yml
.github/workflows/cicd-development.yml
.github/workflows/experimental-deploy.yml
.github/workflows/pr-list-email.yml
.github/scripts/

# --- RAG overlay: now IN this repo (was a private overlay until 2026-08-08) ---
# `src/rag/` and the ask-self command used to be gitignored as the unextracted sleuth-plugin-rag.
# They were audited and carry no keys and no proprietary data: every credential comes from the
# environment (GOOGLE_API_KEY, SLEUTH_RAG_GITHUB_PAT) and the PR corpus repo is env-selected, so
# nothing here names a private repo. They are tracked now — being untracked meant the only copies
# lived in one worktree and on the server.
#
# `chat-module.js` still requires them through the guarded optional seam, which stays: it is what
# lets a clone run clean when the built index is absent. What must NEVER be committed is the index
# itself — see the data/rag/ rules above; the .sqlite is a build artifact of `ingest.mjs`.
/.tick/
